&lt;p&gt;I've been putting together an ACLS lecture script lately: 120 slides, nearly 30,000 characters, all of it in Keynote's speaker notes. When I teach, I keep my laptop on the lectern and turn my head to glance at what comes next after every section.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Sun Can Be Computed, the Clouds Can't: Using AI to Work Out Where to Stand to See the Sun Rise Over Guishan Island</title><link>https://agoodbear.com/en/post/study-post-9/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://agoodbear.com/en/post/study-post-9/</guid><description>
